# CALIB's setup runs from ONE routine (calib_setup_vars, PLAN_CONSOLIDATION 3.3, macos 2026-10-11):
# the LOAD handler's nominal-sensitivity run (OptNomSens= Y) and the CALIB command carried the same
# configuration checks and variable packing as two copies.  A refactor -- TRIPWIRE, no red leg:
# transcripts were byte-identical before and after on tst_calib_nomsens.in (both paths),
# OptAlg= Linear and tst_calib_spot20.in, both compilers.  Pinned here: the nominal path runs at
# LOAD and CALIB then solves (4 iterations, the cap); a deck with no variable element is refused
# by name.
old $ROOT/ZGD_test_files/tst_calib_nomsens.in
calib
no
no
old $ROOT/ZGD_test_files/e5hex1.in
calib
# EXPECT: tst_calib_nomsens\.in\s+being loaded[\s\S]*?Computing nominal system sensitivity[\s\S]*?Optimization iterations =\s+4\s
# EXPECT: e5hex1\.in\s+being loaded[\s\S]*?No Variable Element for Optimization!
